{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1448837-\u00e6on-winged-flight","id":1448837,"title":"[\u00c6on] Winged Flight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-18T03:39:13-07:00","id":1448837,"title":"[\u00c6on] Winged Flight","content":"I'm kinda hoping for an official answer if a Dev is wandering about but I'll also accept something unofficial. So at character creation I took body mod wings because well... I'm doing a dragon girl. Since it only allows flight scale 1 I doubled down and took Q Flight figuring that it would stack and if not I'd at least be able to increase flight speed later. This has led to quite a bit of discussion in the group regarding my flight speed and if I even NEED Q flight. The 2 solutions we came up with were<br /> <br /> - Let Q Flight and winged flight stack as long as Q flight is on putting me at speed scale 2 at base. <br /> - Drop Q flight for mega dex and then get mega-speed and power stunt it as working with wings which would put me at speed scale 1 still but at least let me increase it<br /> - build some Iron Man like boosters to allow a speed increase until I can PROPERLY increase the speed. <br /> <br /> In the end we decided that Q Flight and winged flight can stack for speed scale. How should this situation be handled cause I'm feeling a little burned on the winged character concept cause as far as I can tell winged flight is never meant to be GOOD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26845-seiko","name":"Seiko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T04:44:19-07:00","id":1448840,"title":"","content":"Drop Body Morph Wings, turn into Flight with a restricted (wings) tag, it work the same, but can evolve past 1 dot.<br /> <br /> The powers are about the result and not the aesthetics. So the dot you spent buying Wings can become Flight and evolve from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T16:22:41-07:00","id":1448910,"title":"","content":"You can buy the first level of Flight with a mid-level transformation (physiological shift: wings) to cut the xp cost by six. Further levels would require you to pay full price unless you keep stacking on more transformations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:48:20-07:00","id":1449010,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the Body-Morph wings allows you to utilize flight at no Quantum point cost, whereas the Quantum Power Flight cost quantum points each time you use it. Not sure if this makes a difference for your character, but if there you worry about running out of quantum, it is something to think about. I believe that the interaction with Powers like Quantum Disruption may also be something to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T14:42:34-07:00","id":1449050,"title":"","content":"I would allow it to stack. Why not? In my mind, it would be the same as allowing super-strength 'stack' with Claws, or regular armor stacking with Force Field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T11:31:24-07:00","id":1450704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1448837-\u00e6on-winged-flight?p=1448910#post1448910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can buy the first level of Flight with a mid-level transformation (physiological shift: wings) to cut the xp cost by six. Further levels would require you to pay full price unless you keep stacking on more transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been awhile, but I had ideas for both an expanded explanation of my original suggestion and a hilarious - and almost certainly unintended - alternate method for gaining a winged flight speed.<br /> <br /> Method 1:<br /> <br /> Buy the first level of Flight with a mid-level transformation (physiological shift: wings) to cut the xp cost by six. Buy a second level of Flight and counter the cost via a variant of the Restricted tag to keep your entire Flight power from working unless you're able to spread/flap your wings. You now have Flight 2 and a permanent set of wings for only 6 xp, but need to expend Quantum to fly (unless you buy the Reduced Cost tag twice for 48 xp), and can have your power neutralized (although you still keep the wings).<br /> <br /> Method 2:<br /> <br /> This is the entire reason I bothered posting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Purchase a dot of the Eufiber edge.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Lastly, energized eufiber becomes highly resistant </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">to damage, providing its wearer with armor with </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">the Innocuous and Soft 1 tags, so long as the eufiber </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">contains at least one Quantum point. <u>Add additional </u></span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>armor tags equal to the number of dots in this Edge</u>.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The edge provides no limits on which armor tags can be purchased. Here is a fun one from page 269 of Aeon:</span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Propulsion (1):</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> This armor has some motive pow</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">er allowing it to move in a single medium, like wa</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">ter, land, air, or space. The armor allows the wearer </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">to move at Speed Scale 2 in the medium specified, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">or in space at Space Speed [1] </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(p. 195</span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">). Multiple </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">uses of this tag allow the armor to move in multiple </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">environments.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Yes, RAW does seem to let you spend 3 xp to take a level of the Eufiber edge, granting you cloth wings with Speed Scale 2 in addition to attuned shape changing clothes, a Quantum battery, and a point of Soft, Innocuous armor. I'm not even sure Quantum Disruption could prevent this flight, since it doesn't involve a Power, Mega-Edge, or Mega-Attribute.</span></span> So apparently Eufiber is indeed the greatest Edge ever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 06-02-2021, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T11:50:21-07:00","id":1450706,"title":"","content":"But what causes the propulsion? In Aeon, it's some kind of mechanical propulsion. Eufiber doesn't really have a way of creating mechanical propulsion. And I'd argue since a Nova isn't using a power, if you craft Eufiber into wings, then the wings would need to be able to physically propel you, unlike a quantum power or mega-edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T15:29:02-07:00","id":1450739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1448837-\u00e6on-winged-flight?p=1450706#post1450706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what causes the propulsion? In Aeon, it's some kind of mechanical propulsion. Eufiber doesn't really have a way of creating mechanical propulsion. And I'd argue since a Nova isn't using a power, if you craft Eufiber into wings, then the wings would need to be able to physically propel you, unlike a quantum power or mega-edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that eufiber can change shape means eufiber clothing can generate kinetic force. I can picture a eufiber costume with dragonfly wings that vibrate at greater than hummingbird speeds to provide lift. I'm sure Anibal Buenida would consider it a fashion marvel, and one of their greatest works.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T16:59:49-07:00","id":1450750,"title":"","content":"It changes shape to adapt to the nova's powers. It doesn't move on its own. It takes an action to make it transform, which means you'd have to use an action for each beat of the wings, assuming you had two versions programmed into it, one with the wings back, and one with the wings forward. Otherwise, it would make the Body Modification mega-edge completely obsolete.<br /> <br /> Now, I think most of the Body Modification powers are overly expensive, but I also think they're worth more than 3 xp per power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T18:57:33-07:00","id":1450759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1448837-\u00e6on-winged-flight?p=1450750#post1450750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It changes shape to adapt to the nova's powers. It doesn't move on its own. It takes an action to make it transform, which means you'd have to use an action for each beat of the wings, assuming you had two versions programmed into it, one with the wings back, and one with the wings forward. Otherwise, it would make the Body Modification mega-edge completely obsolete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says clothes can't have moving parts? Eufiber was created by a nova fashion designer, and high fashion can get pretty strange; super powered fashion design is likely even stranger. It also doesn't make alternative methods of flight obsolete since this theoretical method of flight requires the character to be wearing a eufiber costume, which they won't be wearing 24/7.<br /> <br /> Besides which, the little smileys in my post clearly indicate my intent was to demonstrate the absurdity of what you can do when building a character on a RAW reading of the book. I strongly suspect many gaming groups would look askance at such rules cheese being used in their games. Although now I want to make a character with Eufiber 3 so I can take the Defensive (2) tag as well so the character can have a flying porcupine suit. The world needs more flying porcupine suits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T05:33:48-07:00","id":1450801,"title":"","content":"I dont believe you can take tags on enhanced edges. Which Eufiber is @ 6xp a dot. Also, in aberrant things dont necessarily generate forces because they move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10020,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","user":"Manifoldpersona","date":". 06-03-2021, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T05:50:57-07:00","id":1450804,"title":"","content":"Or is it 2? Are nova specific edges normal or enhanced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T07:43:36-07:00","id":1450813,"title":"","content":"as far as I know, Power Tags only apply to &quot;Mega Powers&quot;: Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges (and <i>only </i>Mega-Edges), Quantum Powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T14:55:27-07:00","id":1450886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1448837-\u00e6on-winged-flight?p=1450801#post1450801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont believe you can take tags on enhanced edges. Which Eufiber is @ 6xp a dot. Also, in aberrant things dont necessarily generate forces because they move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eufiber appears to be a normal edge rather than an enhanced edge, and I both quoted part of the edge's text in my original post and underlined the most relevant portion:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>Add additional </u></span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>armor tags equal to the number of dots in this Edge</u>.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>If you've got 1 dot in the Eufiber edge, your costume has one armor tag of your choice. If you've got 5 dots in the Eufiber edge, your costume has five armor tags of your choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}